    <div class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] overflow-hidden mb-6">
        <div class="px-5 py-3 border-b border-white/5">
            <code class="text-cyan-400 text-sm font-semibold">control_metrics(size)</code>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1.5">Box geometry only. The text scale is not here: `size` styles a text node, and only `fg` inherits, so a label takes its size from `control_text_size`. Internal to the catalogue &mdash; it composes part of a widget rather than being called from a view. Documented so the file reads end to end; treat it as implementation detail.</p>
        </div>
<div class="p-4 bg-[#171412] overflow-x-auto">
<pre><code class="language-soli text-sm">base = control_metrics(size).merge({</code></pre>
<p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-3">Real use &mdash; <code>eui_builders.sl (inside `control`):482</code></p>
</div>
